From c8267c90c98031c6e21edcb5346b7457e91505ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:31:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Phonon surface reflection: port G4CMP
 specular/diffuse/anharmonic three-way split

SurfaceProperty stored anh_coeffs and anh_cutoff but never used them, and
specular_prob clamped the frequency at refl_cutoff, so above 350 GHz every
surface stayed 60% specular. G4CMPSurfaceProperty/G4CMPPhononBoundaryProcess
evaluate P_spec, P_diff, P_anh (polynomials below refl_cutoff; P_diff held at
its refl_cutoff value and P_spec = 1 - P_diff - P_anh up to anh_cutoff; above
anh_cutoff P_anh = 0, P_diff = 1 - specProb), normalise, and on the anharmonic
branch down-convert the phonon at the surface (G4CMPAnharmonicDecay::DoDecay)
with both daughters re-emitted Lambertian. With the examples/phonon
coefficients the surface down-conversion probability is 0.04 / 0.15 / 0.47 at
300 / 400 / 500 GHz and the specular probability above 520 GHz is specProb (0),
not 0.60. Added SurfaceProperty::spec_prob_const, reflection_split(), the
surface channel in SimulationEngine::transport, and SimStats::surface_downconversions.
Test: tests/test_surface (probabilities identical to G4CMP; engine branching
fraction within 1%).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BcNoovRae5kkbL36KL3sYy
